course: dictionary
lesson: 15433
title: What are statistics?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Statistics is the branch of maths that collects, organises and studies numbers. Its job is to find patterns and answer questions. «Statistics is my favourite part of maths because it tells us things about the world.» Here it names a school subject, so it takes a singular verb: statistics is.
explain: Statistics can also mean facts shown as numbers. «The statistics show that 300 children visited the library last month.» Here statistics means the numbers themselves, so it is plural and we say the statistics show. One single number or fact is called a statistic: «Our class has 28 pupils» is one statistic.
explain: You meet statistics in tally charts, bar charts, pictograms, line graphs and pie charts. Each one turns numbers into a picture you can read quickly. In science and geography you collect data, then use statistics to compare your results.
fact: Statistics is the branch of maths that collects, organises and studies numbers.
fact: «Statistics» can mean the subject, the numbers themselves, or one single number, which is a «statistic».
fact: Averages such as the mean, median, mode and range are part of statistics.
fact: «Official statistics» are numbers that have been checked and published by an official body.
fact: Statistics help us answer questions, such as «How often does it rain here in May?»
exercise: «Statistics is my favourite part of maths.» What does statistics mean here? | A song about numbers | A football team | *The branch of maths that collects and studies numbers | A type of cake
exercise: «The statistics show that 300 children visited the library.» What does statistics mean in this sentence? | A single person's name | A big school trip to a museum | *Facts shown as numbers | A tall building
exercise: Which word means one single number or fact? | *A statistic | Pictogram | Average | Statistics
test: Which chart uses pictures to show numbers? | Pie chart | Line graph | *Pictogram
test: Which sentence is correct when statistics means the school subject? | Statistics were my favourite subject | *Statistics is my favourite subject | Statistics are my favourite subject
exam: What is a statistic? | A subject taught only in science | A chart with bars | *One number or fact, such as how many pupils are in a class | The name of a type of graph
